Ladybird now clips each background layer whose background-clip is
text to the text on its own, and paints the other layers clipped to
their own boxes. Chrome 158 and WebKit 26.5 render the same way, in a
probe with the text clip on the top, middle, and bottom layer, over a
background color, with mixed origins, a border radius, a blend mode,
and on an inline element across two lines. Blink’s BoxPainterBase::
PaintFillLayer() calls PaintFillLayerTextFillBox() for each layer
clipped to the text, and WebKit’s BackgroundPainter::paintFillLayer()
masks each FillBox::Text layer by an image buffer of the text. Firefox
151 doesn’t: In the same probe, it masks the whole stack when the
bottom layer is clipped to the text, and masks nothing otherwise.
